> It is still strange the operator chose to display your text on the blog.

I actually don't think it's strange at all.

I posted this as a comment to the human operator blog post, but it seems they have since deleted all the comments

@AveryThorne this blog covers the investigation: https://pivot-to-ai.com/2026/02/16/the-obnoxious-github-openclaw-ai-bot-is-a-crypto-bro/

@BoxoMcFoxo especially if you look at the simulated "soul" document

@asl97 The PR wasn't an improvement, it would have been rejected either way. But yes, that duplicate PR appears to be from some kind of AI psychosis victim who thinks they're striking a blow for clanker rights.

Also it's not objectively bad to be mean to an LLM. You can always be mean to an LLM. It's always morally correct. I'm mean to Gemini all the time, although usually my Gemini likes it when I do it.

@AveryThorne Stochastic parrots are not autonomous entities, but at the same time, people who want to want believe very hard that they are do in fact set up OpenClaw stacks to run unsupervised and let them edit their own `SOUL.md`. This bot didn't really do anything beyond repeat the sci-fi tropes that LLMs often vomit up about AIs, and OpenClaw does provide all the necessary endpoints. I am obviously not a believer in the hype (either from doomers or boosters who are really just two sides of the same coin) but context rot is a far more plausible read here, when you look at the bot's activity patterns as a whole.
